 history=top('Our history','An enduring purpose.<br><em>An evolving approach.</em>','The tools change. The purpose remains: economic opportunity that helps alleviate human poverty.')+'''<section class="wrap prose"><div class="timeline"><section><p class="eyebrow">The beginning</p><h2>Fairer access to opportunity</h2><p>Omnequa began by exploring open-source public-benefit blockchain infrastructure, including access to credit, universal basic income and local economies.</p></section><section><p class="eyebrow">Fall 2026</p><h2>Learning from discovery</h2><p>Legal, compliance and impact discovery with nonprofit sponsors and prospective partners concluded in fall 2026.</p><p>The next chapter moved into digital settings, where the team could investigate new economic possibilities directly.</p></section><section><p class="eyebrow">October 2026</p><h2>Exploring the agent economy</h2><p>The team studied credit, payment guarantees and useful work among AI agents. A central insight emerged: most agents have human operators behind their finances.</p></section><section><p class="eyebrow">Our direction today</p><h2>Businesses that benefit people</h2><p>We are exploring how people could own productive AI-assisted businesses, and whether financing real digital work can increase their income while sustaining a growing pool of capital.</p><p>The journal follows these questions in public, with evidence and room to change course.</p></section></div><h2 id="website-archive">The original website journal</h2><p>These October 2026 updates preserve the early work. Their goals and invitations describe that period.</p><ul class="archive-list">'''+archive+'''</ul><p><a href="/archive/evidence/">October goals and reports →</a></p><p class="fine-print">This history does not imply current fiscal sponsorship or charitable status.</p></section>'''
